MUI Native is an independent project by Altroo. It is not an official MUI
product and is not affiliated with or endorsed by MUI.

Material UI and MUI X are names used to identify upstream compatibility targets.
Native rendering code is independently authored. Palette, color, spacing,
breakpoint, typography, default/slot-prop, slot routing, ref lifecycle, input/adornment state, label/helper state/layout, nested/scoped theme providers, modal/focus coordination, transition timing/lifecycle and height-based opacity/scale, reduced-motion configuration, container text inheritance, anchored popover positioning, ButtonBase activation, list composition and responsive-style algorithms adapt
MIT-licensed Material UI/System/Utils
code as recorded in upstream/reuse.json. Native registered menu navigation,
initial focus, typeahead, anchored Menu slot/focus composition, slot identifiers
and icon inheritance also adapt these contracts. Select value matching, closed
typeahead, display/width policy, native selection events and TextField select
composition adapt the same MIT-licensed references. Checkbox/Radio/Switch state,
input events, label/group and five-slot switch composition, motion and slot identifiers also adapt those
MIT-licensed references. Chip slot, activation/deletion, label and style contracts
also adapt those MIT-licensed references; native glyph geometry is independently authored.
Popper wrapper, slots, refs, RTL and transition/instance composition also adapt
those MIT-licensed references. Autocomplete filtering, value mapping, state transitions,
component/slot composition and public contracts also adapt those MIT-licensed
references; native scrolling and indicator geometry are independently authored. Upstream public declaration
snapshots and license texts are retained under upstream/. Derived declaration
inventories are retained under compatibility/inventory/. Their applicable MIT
notices are preserved in upstream/licenses/. No Pro or Premium source, assets,
license checks, or paid-only feature implementations are included.

Upstream source references, package integrity values, and source commits are
recorded in upstream/state.json. Baseline copiedFiles lists reuse at the initial
snapshot; later implementation adaptations are recorded in upstream/reuse.json.

